Button prompt style setting, game.buttonPrompts = gamecube | playstation (the Vita
defaults to playstation). With playstation the button textures are swapped for
glyphs the platform draws itself (twilight-vita: platform/vita/ui/ps_glyphs.cpp,
our own shapes, no console artwork):
- layout textures where every layout resolves them by name: JUTResReference
  (BLO materials and pictures) and J2DScreen::getNameResource (texture changes
  by name). This covers the HUD buttons, the button guides and the menus. Only
  an explicit list of button textures is swapped, and only when the texture
  came from an archive that holds that button (its root name) and has the
  expected format and size;
- in-text icons by icon number in COutFont_c::createPane, drawn with a neutral
  tint instead of the GameCube colours;
- the main HUD (zelda_game_image) and its button guide (button_info): once
  built, their button bases take a dark colour and the face-button symbols
  their own (cross blue, circle red, square pink, triangle green), through
  the pictures' black/white colours only.
With gamecube, or without platform glyphs, every lookup returns the original
resource.

